Editor Keys:
LEFT/RIGHT - Turn left and right.
A/D - Strafe left and right.
W/S - Move forward and back.
Q - Quit.
Hold SHIFT - Speed up movement.
Hold middle mouse button - Forward/back movement and strafing by mouse
                           movements.
Hold right mouse button - Turning by mouse movements.
Click left mouse button - Select point, line and sector.

If an action would affect just a floor or ceiling, which one is determined by
whether the cursor is on the top or bottom half of the window when the action
is first initiated, not when completed, in the case of an action which
requests more input.

If the editor isn't waiting for text entry or selection of another object:
J - Point mode:
      Join 2 lines on sides of point together.
    Line mode:
      Join 2 sectors on sides of line together.
X - Point mode:
      Requires selecting a second point, then splits a sector in to 2 along
      the line formed between the 2 points.
    Line mode:
      Splits a line at the midpoint in to 2 lines.
L - Line mode:
      Link 2 lines on 2 sectors which are both sharing the same 2 common
      points, allowing to see through to each other sector.
U - Line mode:
      Unlink sectors from 2 lines, making a wall between the two sectors.
M - Point mode:
      Move a point, will affect all lines sharing the point, CTRL+M if this
      isn't desired.
CTRL+M - Point mode:
            Move a point independently of anything else sharing the point.
CTRL+S - Sector mode:
           Solidify sector, deletes the sector, making it in to a wall.
T - In line or sector mode, requires entering in a new texture number, then
    sets the wall or sector texture to that.
H - Like T but shade.  Shade is given as 3 numbers from 0-3 for RGB, 'p' as
    first character to display as parallax.  Negative numbers do subtractive
    blending instead of additive.
CTRL+H - Sector mode:
           Adjust ceiling or floor height.
B - Like T but for bias (texture offset), requires entering a new 2x2 matrix.
R - like T but for transform (texture transformed based on world coordinates).
      Line mode:
        Requires entering a new 3x2 matrix (world X, Y and height Z in to
        texture X, Y).
      Sector mode:
        Requires entering a new 2x2 matrix (world X, Y in to texture X, Y).
I - Print information on any highlighted item in the current mode.
TAB - Change target mode for actions between point, line and sector modes.
      Also affects which is highlighted for selection and cursor hover.
      Selection is based on which sector the cursor is over or which sector
      the wall the cursor is hovered over belongs to, which line the cursor is
      over or on the nearest ahead on the pixel column the cursor is on, and
      the point which is on the selected line and is nearest to the cursor.

If the editor is waiting for text entry or selection of another object:
ESC - Cancel operation and stop waiting for additional parameters.
